        <mxCell id="-ytKBwrGRmqnR_m710Oe-33" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="NOTE: Changes made to any of the file&#39;s chunks will reflect in the file&#39;s last modified at timestamp too&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Reasoning being, the sync feature would require me to fetch from DB the list of all files which changed after specific timestamp x.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="528" x="20" y="1093" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="-ytKBwrGRmqnR_m710Oe-34" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="GET /changes?since={timestamp}" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="60" x="-320" y="1846" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="-ytKBwrGRmqnR_m710Oe-35" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Response:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;FileMetadata[] for all files changed after the given timestamp&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The client can then call the GET {S3 Presigned URL} to download the blob content&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="156" width="265" x="-327" y="1927" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="-ytKBwrGRmqnR_m710Oe-38" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Client&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;• On the upload path, client does chunking and compression of data. Computes&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;fingerprint hash of each chunk, save in metadata DB and u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;pload them in parallel to S3&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;• On the download path, fetches the file metadata, downloads the chunks from S3, decompresses them and combine into the single file.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
